& [JustificationIdentity] is the Phase6 SJS rationale
  + [justification_uuid] is 9d163caa-e11c-487b-aa18-550797523e52
  + [reserved_solution_uuid] is a6fe47fc-54bd-443a-af25-9deff7d58896

& [Problem] is physical persistence remains an intuition rather than an evidence-backed requirement
  + [current_fact] is the executable semantic fabric is reconstructed in memory from a signed environment
  + [risk] is selecting an RDBMS for imagined scale may freeze the wrong physical model and enlarge the trusted operational surface
  + [counter_risk] is refusing to measure may hide a genuine startup, update, inspection, or corpus-management requirement

& [SelectedApproach] is a disposable comparative lab
  + [why] is candidate dependencies and schemas remain outside production while exact Cantor objects supply the oracle
  + [why] is JSON, SQLite, and redb span transparent snapshot, relational application file, and pure-Rust key-value designs
  + [why] is multiple package counts expose structural trends without a production-scale claim

& [Alternative] is adopt SQLite immediately
  + [rejected_for_now] is present normalized relational query and concurrent-update requirements are not yet implemented or measured

& [Alternative] is adopt redb immediately
  + [rejected_for_now] is exact-key speed alone does not establish a need for a persistent key-value engine or its format commitment

& [Alternative] is keep JSON without comparison
  + [rejected] is it would preserve simplicity but leave the next architecture decision unmeasured

& [RiskTreatment] is explicit
  + [cache_bias] is results named warm reopen and reconstruction
  + [synthetic_bias] is package generator and unit-per-package shape recorded
  + [corruption] is every load checked through digest equality, admission, and exact response equality
  + [dependency] is experiment has a separate lockfile and no production dependency activation
  + [adoption] is experiment result may defer backend selection
